hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27985","Affan narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Khubayb, he said: I heard my paternal aunt saying, she having performed Hajj with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say: Ibn Umm Maktum calls at night, so eat and drink until Bilal calls; or: Bilal calls at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls. One would ascend and the other descend, so we would cling to him and say: As you are, until we take the predawn meal."
"27986","Hushaym narrated to us: Mansur, meaning Ibn Zadahn, narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his paternal aunt Unaysah bint Khubayb, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When Ibn Umm Maktum calls, eat and drink; and when Bilal calls, do not eat nor drink. She said: And a woman would still have of her predawn meal left, so we would say to Bilal: Wait until I finish my predawn meal."
"27987","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his paternal aunt, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Ibn Umm Maktum, or Bilal, calls at night, so eat and drink until Bilal, or Ibn Umm Maktum, calls. There was only that one of them would call and the other ascend, so we would take him by his hand and say: As you are, until we take the predawn meal."
